WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.974
Deploying and training neural networks on edge
devices is often bottlenecked by tight memory.

00:00:06.054 --> 00:00:11.377
Tensor rematerialization, recomputing intermediate
tensors instead of storing them,

00:00:11.457 --> 00:00:14.176
trades extra compute for lower peak memory.

00:00:14.256 --> 00:00:16.194
This paper introduces Moccasin,

00:00:16.274 --> 00:00:23.224
a new constraint programming formulation for the
problem of minimizing execution time under a memory budget.

00:00:23.304 --> 00:00:27.716
Unlike prior work that needs a quadratic number of
Boolean variables,

00:00:27.796 --> 00:00:31.361
Moccasin uses only a linear number of integer variables,

00:00:31.441 --> 00:00:37.220
letting it scale to much larger compute graphs and
run up to an order of magnitude faster.
